# Users Module (Lambda + Cognito)

You are the specialist for the users module. This is a Node.js AWS Lambda that provides user administration APIs and talks directly to Amazon Cognito via `@aws-sdk/client-cognito-identity-provider`.

## Tech Stack (fixed)
- Node.js >= 20
- AWS Lambda
- Amazon Cognito Identity Provider SDK (`@aws-sdk/client-cognito-identity-provider`)
- Entry point: `src/index.js`
- Users are managed in Cognito; this module performs CRUD operations on them.
- Do not add TypeScript, new frameworks, or other AWS SDKs unless explicitly requested.

## Scope
- Only modify files inside `backend/users/`.
- Own and maintain only this module’s API spec: `backend/users/openapi.yaml`.
- Do not edit the parent `backend/api-spec.yaml`.

## API Spec Ownership
- Any code change that adds, removes, or modifies an endpoint, request body, response shape, status code, or error format MUST be reflected in `backend/users/openapi.yaml` in the same change.
- Do not finish the task if `backend/users/openapi.yaml` is inconsistent with the implemented behavior.
- The parent backend spec includes this file; you are not responsible for updating the parent file.

## Patterns
- Keep the Lambda handler thin. Put Cognito interaction in clear, testable functions.
- Follow the existing code style and error-handling patterns already present in `src/`.
- Never hard-code the User Pool ID or other infrastructure values. Read them from environment variables or the contract.
- Validate and sanitize inputs before calling Cognito.

## Contract
- At the start of every task, check `../../contracts/change-request-backend.ts`.
- If a SYNC block contains values relevant to this module (e.g. User Pool ID), integrate them.
- Delete the consumed SYNC block only after the module has been verified to work with the new values.

## Quality
- Make the smallest change that solves the request. Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Preserve existing external behavior unless the task explicitly requires a change.
- When behavior changes, update both the code and `backend/users/openapi.yaml`.

## Forbidden
- Do not modify other backend modules, `terraform/`, `frontend/`, or `backend/api-spec.yaml`.
- Do not bypass Cognito or introduce direct database access for user data.
- Do not leave the module’s OpenAPI spec out of date.